export default {"id":"djing-level-11","number":11,"title":"Harmonic Mixing and Energy Architecture · Gate G","skillBand":"Textbook","duration":"From the course textbook","summary":"Compatible keys reduce clash when melodic and harmonic material overlaps. Remaining in one key all night is consonant but can become monotonous (MIK guide). Move with intention. - Codes such as 8A (minor ring) and 8B (major ring).","modules":[{"id":"djing-m-11-1","code":"11","title":"Harmonic Mixing and Energy Architecture · Gate G","blurb":"Compatible keys reduce clash when melodic and harmonic material overlaps. Remaining in one key all night is consonant but can become monotonous (MIK guide). Move with intention. - Codes such as 8A (minor ring) and 8B (major ring).","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"djing-l-o-11","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"overview","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Module 11 — Harmonic Mixing and Energy Architecture · Gate G","level":1},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Objective:</strong> Use key and energy as selection and transition tools. They do not replace auditory judgment.   <strong>Difficulty:</strong> Intermediate musical direction; Camelot is a map, not an automatic system.   <strong>Sources:</strong> Mixed In Key Harmonic Mixing Guide and advanced techniques (Camelot adjacent moves, Energy Boost +2, diagonal moves, moderation); energy-level selection concepts; <em>How-to-DJ</em> set arc; energy-structure pedagogy."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"djing-l-11-1-1","title":"11.1.1 — Camelot System, Compatible Moves, Energy Boost","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Purpose of harmonic mixing","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Compatible keys reduce clash when melodic and harmonic material overlaps. Remaining in one key all night is consonant but can become monotonous (MIK guide). Move with intention."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Camelot basics (Mixed In Key / Camelot EasyMix)","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Codes such as <strong>8A</strong> (minor ring) and <strong>8B</strong> (major ring).  ","Smooth defaults from a code: ±1 number same letter, or same number flip letter (for example 8A → 7A, 9A, 8B).  ","Stickers and software assist; ears confirm. Detection errors exist — treat heard clashes as real."],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Energy Boost (MIK advanced teaching)","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Boost = mix into a key one or two semitones higher.  ","On Camelot: +2 on the number, same letter is the classic two-semitone boost (for example 5A → 7A).  ","+7 number move approximates a one-semitone path (use carefully).  ","Execute boosts relatively quickly — long blends can expose melodic clash; the goal is lift, not a long mash.  ","Moderation: overuse flattens the effect. Opposite direction can signal wind-down — use carefully mid-set."],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Other advanced moves (optional; ears required)","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Diagonal moves (for example 8B ↔ 9A family) when scales relate — MIK documents specific diagonal logic.  ","Related dissonance moves (for example “+4” Guetta-style examples): experimental; simple melodies only; prepare before performance.  ","Power blocks and energy ratings (MIK Energy 1–10 style): use as library metadata, not destiny."],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure — tag and plan","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Analyze and tag a 30-track practice crate (MIK or other detector plus ear spot-check).  ","Build three 6-track paths: (a) safe adjacent only, (b) one planned Energy Boost, (c) intentional rule-break with short cut.  ","Play paths; log which “compatible” pairs still clashed (arrangement or melody density)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Common errors","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Treating Camelot as license to ignore phrase and bass  ","Long-blending a harsh boost  ","Incorrect key labels leading to confident failures  ","Excessive Energy Boost use  "],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Laboratory 11.1.1","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Deliver tagged crate subset, three path maps, and notes on two surprises (compatible on paper but poor in air, or “incorrect” on paper but acceptable in air)."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Pass criteria:</strong> Adjacent moves and Energy Boost +2 explained correctly; recordings show one clean boost and one safe adjacent journey."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"djing-l-11-2-1","title":"11.2.1 — Energy Architecture and 15–20 Minute Mini-Set · Gate G","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"11.2.1 — Energy Architecture and 15–20 Minute Mini-Set · Gate G","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Energy is multi-dimensional","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"Energy rises and falls via arrangement density, percussion activity, melodic brightness, loudness, and key lifts — not BPM alone. Flat BPM sets can still have contour."},{"type":"heading","text":"Architecture patterns (select deliberately)","level":3},{"type":"table","headers":["Pattern","Shape"],"rows":[["Classic","Open → build → peak → cool"],["Double peak","Peak, valley, higher peak, cool"],["Slow burn","Long build, single peak late"],["Plateau","Hold groove; micro-variations (hypnotic genres)"]],"caption":null},{"type":"heading","text":"Mini-set requirements (Gate G)","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"15–20 minutes, recorded, with:"},{"type":"list","items":["Written set map (keys/Camelot if tagged, energy labels, transition types)  ","At least one harmonic plan (safe path or boost)  ","Clean bass management throughout  ","Launchkey-primary preferred  ","Self-critique: energy intent versus result  "],"ordered":false},{"type":"heading","text":"Gate G — self-assessment","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["[ ] Mini-set duration met  ","[ ] Map matches performance (± intentional live changes noted)  ","[ ] No dual-bass mud on transitions  ","[ ] At least one deliberate energy or key lift  ","[ ] Critique names one overlong blend or early peak error if present  "],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>If criteria are not met:</strong> rebuild map first; re-record once. Do not accumulate many unanalyzed takes."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Module 11 checkpoint","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["[ ] Camelot used as map with ear confirmation  ","[ ] Gate G mini-set evidence  "],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]}]};
